LOG BOOK ENTRY — SECTION 23: DARK MATTER SUBSTRUCTURE

Hours Worked: 7 hours
Date: April 26, 2026
Author: Abhinav Vatsa

--------------------------------------------
OBJECTIVE
--------------------------------------------
Analyze dark matter substructure in the MW–M31 merger simulation using a Friends-of-Friends (FoF) clustering algorithm to identify, track, and quantify subhalos over time.

--------------------------------------------
WORK COMPLETED
--------------------------------------------

1. IMPLEMENTED FOF SUBHALO FINDER
- Built grid-accelerated Friends-of-Friends algorithm
- Linking length: 2.0 kpc
- Minimum group size: 30 particles
- Used union-find structure with path compression for efficiency

2. SUBHALO IDENTIFICATION
- Extracted subhalo candidates across multiple snapshots
- Filtered physically meaningful structures (10^8–10^12 M☉)
- Excluded dominant main halo contamination

3. PHYSICAL QUANTITIES COMPUTED
For each subhalo:
- Total mass
- Center-of-mass position
- Radial distance from system COM
- Velocity dispersion (mass-weighted 3D)

4. TEMPORAL EVOLUTION TRACKING
- Tracked subhalo population across ~80 snapshots
- Measured:
  • Subhalo count vs time
  • Total and mean subhalo mass
  • Velocity dispersion evolution

5. SUBHALO MASS FUNCTION (SHMF)
- Constructed cumulative distribution N(>M)
- Fitted power-law slope α(t)
- Compared with CDM expectation α ≈ -1
- Observed temporal deviations during merger phases

6. RADIAL DISTRIBUTION ANALYSIS
- Computed n_sub(r) profiles
- Confirmed strong radial anti-bias
- Outer halo retains higher subhalo survival fraction

7. KINEMATIC ANALYSIS
- Compared subhalo vs field velocity dispersion
- Identified tidal heating effects
- Quantified kinematic bias in subhalo population

8. SPATIAL STRUCTURE VISUALIZATION
- Generated 2D x–y subhalo maps
- Marker size scaled with log mass
- Tracked morphological evolution over time

9. OUTPUT PRODUCTS GENERATED
- SHMF evolution plots
- Radial density profiles
- Subhalo survival curves
- Mass + velocity evolution plots
- 2D maps across epochs
- Full animation (mp4)
- Summary diagnostic panel

--------------------------------------------
KEY RESULTS
--------------------------------------------
- Subhalo population declines during merger pericenter passages
- Low-mass subhalos are preferentially disrupted
- SHMF slope steepens temporarily from CDM expectation
- Strong radial dependence confirms tidal stripping dominance
- Outer halo preserves long-lived substructure
- Evidence of kinematic heating in surviving subhalos
